  "id": "auditory-verbal-learning-test",
  "term": "Auditory Verbal Learning Test",
  "definition": "The Auditory Verbal Learning Test is a neuropsychological assessment that uses a spoken list of words longer than immediate memory span to evaluate verbal memory and learning. It can provide measures such as short-term recall, learning across repeated trials, and delayed recall, and is used to help detect memory impairment.",
